### GitFix AI REST API Collection

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@connectionId = replace-with-connection-id
@jobId = replace-with-job-id

### 1. Actuator Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

### 2. Register a New GitHub Connection
# Encrypts PAT using AES-GCM and generates a per-connection webhook secret
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/connections
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "githubToken": "ghp_yourPersonalAccessTokenHere",
  "repoFullName": "your-username/your-repo-name"
}

### 3. List All Active Connections
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/connections
Accept: application/json

### 4. Get Connection by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/connections/{{connectionId}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. Auto-Register GitHub Webhook on Target Repository
# Automatically registers http://<public-url>/api/webhook/github/{connectionId} via GitHub API
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/connections/{{connectionId}}/webhook
Accept: application/json

### 6. Trigger Job Manually (Handy for testing without webhook)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/manual
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "connectionId": "{{connectionId}}",
  "issueNumber": 1
}

### 7. List All Jobs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs
Accept: application/json

### 8. Get Job Details by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/{{jobId}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Get Job Execution Logs (Step-by-step audit)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/{{jobId}}/logs
Accept: application/json

### 10. Get Job Attempts & Patch Diffs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/{{jobId}}/attempts
Accept: application/json

### 11. Retry a Failed Job
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/{{jobId}}/retry
Accept: application/json

### 12. Delete a Connection
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/connections/{{connectionId}}
Accept: application/json
